WEBVTT

00:00.640 --> 00:04.960
If your purpose is your why, your vision is your where.

00:08.400 --> 00:15.280
Now, a common question we get is, do I need one M.V.P. blueprint for my personal life

00:15.280 --> 00:23.760
and then another for my professional life? The answer is no. An athlete leads one integrated life.

00:24.640 --> 00:31.920
It's important to know that drafting this vision takes time and you should expect to have

00:31.920 --> 00:39.760
several iterations. Don't aim for perfection. Aim for progress because when you get clear on your

00:39.760 --> 00:46.480
vision and you're able to share it, it builds a powerful foundation of trust with your team.

00:47.440 --> 00:53.840
Your vision is the ability to look ahead and see with vivid detail the future you're working to

00:53.840 --> 01:02.080
create. It's the destination of your leadership map. A vision isn't a vague dream like,

01:02.080 --> 01:09.120
I want to be successful. It's a clear written declaration. A powerful vision is sensory.

01:09.120 --> 01:15.280
What do you see? What do you hear? Who is around you? How do you feel? For example,

01:15.280 --> 01:22.320
a vision statement might be, in five years I will be leading a global team recognized as an expert

01:22.320 --> 01:29.840
in sustainable technology while maintaining the flexibility of being fully present for my family.

01:29.840 --> 01:38.080
It's specific. It's aspirational. It provides daily motivation. When the day-to-day work gets

01:38.080 --> 01:46.160
tough, when you face a setback, you can close your eyes and see the vision. It reminds you

01:46.160 --> 01:53.600
of what you're fighting for. It's what helps an athlete push through that last painful mile of

01:53.600 --> 02:00.640
that marathon. They aren't thinking about the pain. They're visualizing the final finish line.

02:01.280 --> 02:07.440
In your playbook, you will use the reflections you did in lesson two on your desire to feature

02:07.440 --> 02:14.720
state to draft a powerful vision statement. Now, don't be afraid to dream big. An athlete's

02:14.720 --> 02:25.360
vision should stretch them. It should pull you forward.

